  "sourceFitAssessment": {
    "learnerTask": "Compare PD-1/PD-L1/PD-L2 with CD28/CTLA-4 shared-ligand contacts",
    "gap": "Table and outcome flow omit distinct molecular contacts and nonexclusive sites",
    "accuracyGuardrails": "blocking PD-L1 not PD-L2; no HLA restoration or all-cell awakening; tissue injury possible",
    "baselinePageSHA256": "897599158cfddce62e1b257773b563fe1f82b74d94d15602aa23a9a0899850e9",
    "currentVisualFit": "adequate",
    "humanReview": "pending",
    "reasoning": "PD-1 is drawn with PD-L1 and PD-L2 as distinct partners. The selected PD-L1 contact alone is crossed out, while PD-L2 remains directly unblocked. A separate pair shows CD28 and CTLA-4 sharing CD80/CD86, labeled supporting versus limiting signals. The original capture/signaling artwork remains retained; this extension adds partner inventory and contact-specific blockade without redrawing capture. Overlapping sites, absent HLA restoration, lack of universal awakening and possible tissue injury are stated next to the visual. These meet the frozen molecular-contact task without implying interchangeable drugs or guaranteed response."
  },
